# Plan: implement `rb_create`

## Context

`src/rbtree.c` defines `struct rbtree` and `struct rb_node` but contains no
functions yet. The first one to build is `rb_create`, the constructor every
other operation and every test depends on. Its contract (`include/rbtree.h:8`):

```c
rbtree_t *rb_create(rb_value_free_fn value_free);
/* Returns NULL on allocation failure.
 * value_free may be NULL (values not owned). */
```

Scope for this change (per user): **`rb_create` only**, plus the `#include`
it requires. `rb_destroy` and a test harness are out of scope, so end-to-end
`make test` / `asan` / `memcheck` cannot exercise this yet — verification is a
standalone compile check.

## Design

Two heap allocations, so the CLAUDE.md **goto-cleanup** rule applies:

1. `malloc` the `struct rbtree`.
2. `malloc` the shared `nil` sentinel node (matches the existing struct field
   `rb_node_t *nil;` and the comments already in the file — one sentinel per
   tree, allocated here, freed once by `rb_destroy` later).
3. Initialise the sentinel: `color = BLACK`; `key`/`value = NULL`;
   `parent`/`left`/`right` point at the sentinel itself (self-referential, so a
   stray traversal terminates rather than dereferencing NULL).
4. Initialise the tree: `root = nil` (empty tree is `root == nil`, never NULL),
   `value_free = value_free` (stored verbatim, NULL allowed), `size = 0`.
5. On sentinel allocation failure: `free` the tree and return `NULL`. The tree
   is left untouched from the caller's view (nothing was returned), matching
   "NULL return leaves the tree unchanged".

### Code to add to `src/rbtree.c`

Prerequisite include (after the existing `<stdio.h>` / `<stdlib.h>`):

```c
#include "rbtree.h"
```

Needed for `rbtree_t`, `rb_value_free_fn`, and `size_t`. See the notes in the
git history of this plan file for exactly what `#include` pulls in.

The function (placed after the `struct rbtree` definition):

```c
rbtree_t *rb_create(rb_value_free_fn value_free) {
    rbtree_t *t = malloc(sizeof *t);
    if (t == NULL) {
        return NULL;
    }

    rb_node_t *nil = malloc(sizeof *nil);
    if (nil == NULL) {
        goto fail_tree;
    }
    nil->key = NULL;
    nil->value = NULL;
    nil->color = BLACK;
    nil->parent = nil;
    nil->left = nil;
    nil->right = nil;

    t->nil = nil;
    t->root = nil;
    t->value_free = value_free;
    t->size = 0;
    return t;

fail_tree:
    free(t);
    return NULL;
}
```

No loops, so no invariant comments required. A short block comment above the
function restating the contract is appropriate to match existing style.

## Files

- `src/rbtree.c` — add `#include "rbtree.h"`; add the `rb_create` definition.

## Verification

Full `make test` / `make asan` / `make memcheck` cannot run yet (empty
`tests/test_rbtree.c` has no `main`, so the test binary will not link; leak
checks also need `rb_destroy`). Instead:

- Compile-check the translation unit with the project's exact flags:
  `gcc -std=c23 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -g -O1 -Iinclude -c src/rbtree.c -o /dev/null`
  — must produce no warnings or errors. This proves the `#include` resolves the
  missing `rb_value_free_fn` symbol and that `rb_create` is well-formed.
- Re-run the three `make` targets as the next functions (`rb_destroy`, then a
  smoke test) land; do not consider `rb_create` fully "DONE" per CLAUDE.md until
  all three pass with a test that calls it.
- No commit from this state (not green per the project rule); commit once a
  green `make test` is reachable.

